WEBVTT

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.540
I was born in London.

00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:14.950
My home was just the slightest
bit different from the norm.

00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:18.290
My dad was a detective,
while my mum was a thief.

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:23.660
Being born from this union meant
I inherited abilities from both of them.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:28.120
From my father I learned the art
of observation, mind-reading,

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.750
languages of the world, and human psychology.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.580
From my mother I learned how to disable
a trap, find someone's blind spot,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.250
and how to charm and manipulate others.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.700
But my parents didn't tell me to
take up either of their professions.

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:49.790
They insisted I figure out for myself
how I'd make a living.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:55.750
When I was 15, my parents died in a plane crash.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:04.290
Once I was alone, I realized: I had never
made a single decision on my own.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:08.870
And now, I couldn't even choose how to live.

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:11.540
How should I go on living?

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:17.160
It was then, at my wits' end,
that I found it in my father's study.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:24.080
My father had been asked to uncover
secrets in a certain game.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:27.500
More than anything else,
my desire to choose welled up inside.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.000
What was this game's slogan again?

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:39.370
Surely no words ever sounded so attractive
to someone who lacked direction.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:45.870
Then I guess I'll take them up
on that offer, that new world.

00:01:45.870 --> 00:01:49.500
I hope they can show me the way--

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:52.250
to my possibilities.

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:53.700
Let's do this.

00:03:25.580 --> 00:03:27.450
Motor Slash!

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.890
"Chapter 11:
 The Right Arm of the Victor"

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:33.160
Babi. Little Flare.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:34.870
Roger that!

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.330
Now he'll step with his right leg.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.450
An upward slice with his left blade.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:49.290
Liz. Move.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:54.200
Marilyn--attack!

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.580
Aggravating.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.160
It's like he's anticipating our every move.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:02.660
No--he <i>is</i> .

00:04:02.660 --> 00:04:06.080
If this continues, we'll be
the first to run out of steam.

00:04:06.080 --> 00:04:07.950
And yet...

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:12.370
How long can you withstand this
La Porte de l'Enfer without freezing?

00:04:12.370 --> 00:04:17.290
I freeze about the same amount every time,
but the intervals are all over the place.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:21.870
The second hit of Frozen came
39 seconds after the first.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:26.750
The third went into effect
130 seconds after that.

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.870
That's a greatest common divisor of 13.

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.200
There has to be some kind
of meaning behind that number.

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:38.370
Liz. I need to think, so you concentrate
on evasion and defense.

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.250
So there are three types of Frozen:

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:42.370
A gradual freezing over time,

00:04:42.370 --> 00:04:45.870
like what happened to me and Audrey.

00:04:47.660 --> 00:04:50.040
Who was instantaneously half-Frozen at first.

00:04:50.040 --> 00:04:54.870
Then there are the Masters who were
flash-Frozen in their entirety.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:59.120
And there are those like Babi and
Marilyn who don't freeze at all.

00:04:59.120 --> 00:05:02.790
What is it that makes one
get Frozen? Is it only humans?

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:05.870
Negative: Audrey's Frozen.

00:05:05.870 --> 00:05:09.660
Does it have a greater effect on targets
with better stats or higher levels?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:13.250
Negative: That doesn't explain the difference
between Audrey and Marilyn,

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.080
with similar numbers.

00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:17.950
Maybe it's a randomized power fluctuation.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:23.290
Negative: Luck-based skills aren't ideal
for defending strategic locations.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:26.000
There's <i>got</i> to be some kind of rule behind it.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.540
Rook! Look out!

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:34.500
Two seconds till I take a hit.

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.330
No dodging this one.

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.790
In which case...

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:40.160
Let's approach this from another angle.

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.000
An Embryo's name and its skill aren't unrelated.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.500
Cocytus was the frozen hell of treachery
in Dante's <i>Divine Comedy</i> ,

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:52.700
where Satan, trapped in ice,
eternally gnawed on traitors.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.950
Could there be a deeper connection here,

00:05:55.950 --> 00:05:58.750
apart from Frozen hitting
at intervals divisible by 13?

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:03.330
What makes it a hell?
What makes an act traitorous?

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:08.330
If there were some kind of treachery
that could be expressed in numbers, then--

00:06:08.330 --> 00:06:09.870
Expressed in numbers?

00:06:09.870 --> 00:06:13.870
I know that number. It exists!

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:19.160
It can be interpreted as betrayal <i>and</i>
can be linked to the difference in effect!

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.870
I get it now: La Porte de l'Enfer is counting--

00:06:25.580 --> 00:06:27.200
Rook?!

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.450
It's over.

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:31.790
No...

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:34.750
Not yet.

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:39.000
This is where I defeat you.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.700
For a Pimp, you're far too sturdy.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.250
All thanks to Ray.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:54.250
You were lucky to withstand that.
It won't happen again.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:58.200
Besides, La Porte de l'Enfer
continues to consume you.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:06:59.950
That's true.

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:04.370
You could say your skill has me in check.

00:07:04.370 --> 00:07:10.620
After all, I took down a number of humans myself
in the plaza battle against the player killers.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.080
What are you saying?

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.870
La Porte de l'Enfer has different
effects depending on the kill count

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:20.700
for creatures of your same type.

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.080
Seven humans, eh?

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.660
Yes, I'd say about seven percent
of my body is Frozen each time.

00:07:27.660 --> 00:07:32.450
Every 13 seconds, La Porte de l'Enfer
has an x percent chance

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.910
of rendering x percent of the
selected target's body Frozen.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:38.660
Does that sound about right?

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:43.250
In my case, there's a seven percent
chance every 13 seconds

00:07:43.250 --> 00:07:47.120
that seven percent of my body will be Frozen.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:52.700
A frozen hell for those traitors
who killed their fellow creatures.

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:55.870
It also explains why you're
stationed by the escape route.

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:02.580
Nice deductive work, but maybe
the conditions just happened to fit.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.370
I can tell by your voice that I'm right.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:10.000
You're a terrible liar.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.620
And <i>that's</i> why I hate you.

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:18.830
I hate people who are so obvious with their
inner doubts, their deception--like you.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:19.790
What?

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:26.250
You're like Ray: You see this world
as a <i>world</i> , not as a game, right?

00:08:26.250 --> 00:08:28.330
And yet, your actions...

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.910
It's all so <i>irritating</i> .

00:08:30.910 --> 00:08:36.000
Irritating that you're a party to Franklin's
game, complicit in this tragedy--

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.660
and then wave it off, all, "I must,"
and, "This is the only way."

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:43.040
Your words and your attitude speak volumes.

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.290
Irritating that you try to justify
your actions, yet preface it with,

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:50.910
"I'm such a terrible person,"
making excuses for your excuses.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:56.410
Irritating that, as indecisive as you are,
you would still hold Ray back.

00:08:56.410 --> 00:09:02.000
Irritating that you're so tormented by
your guilt, even as you wallow in it!

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:07.040
Speaking of, you're so full of yourself with
your over-the-top turns of phrase--irritating!

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.790
You irritate the <i>hell</i> out of me!

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:14.450
And your Magingear's churchy
design is irritating, too!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:17.200
We are <i>done</i> !

00:09:17.200 --> 00:09:21.330
Your attitude, an even more awful take
on that of a certain someone,

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:24.370
is supremely irritating <i>and</i> loathsome.

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:27.660
Yuh... You...

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:30.540
You're too indecisive, <i>miss</i> .

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:33.200
Damn you!

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:36.450
Union Jack.

00:09:49.370 --> 00:09:51.290
Wh-Who <i>are</i> you?

00:09:51.290 --> 00:09:52.620
Are you--?

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:55.330
Union Jack: Dragon-Devil-Man!

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.450
Little Flare.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:03.580
This must be the magic skill his Embryo used!

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:05.790
Tri-Horn Uppercut!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:08.500
Is this that Demi-Dragon's attack?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.160
Any more, and--

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:16.870
Motor Slash!

00:10:16.870 --> 00:10:19.700
He dodged that <i>blind</i> ?

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.620
So they've merged together.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:26.120
A skill of that caliber, and he can
use it with no preparation?

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:29.040
Oh, I've been preparing all along.

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:33.040
Now, exactly when do you think
I started my preparations, hmm?

00:10:33.040 --> 00:10:34.330
When?

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:38.540
Turns out it was <i>me</i> who had <i>you</i> in check.

00:10:38.540 --> 00:10:42.370
You could say your skill has me in check.

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.250
We are <i>done</i> !

00:10:44.250 --> 00:10:50.040
I see... So that irritating speech he gave,
insulting me--he was buying time!

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.370
Right now, my creature type is "chimera."

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:57.080
Since I've never defeated a chimera,
La Porte de l'Enfer has no effect on me.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:11:00.790
So now it's just a sheer contest of might...

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.870
Hugo Lesseps!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:07.910
A contest of might? Very well, Rook Holmes!

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:20.660
Tri-Horn... Grand Dash!

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:22.370
Purgatorial Slash!

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:52.580
I didn't have... the power to win...

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:54.450
That was a close call.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:57.120
Yes, it was--

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.950
Thanks, Liz.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.290
Male Temptation.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:10.330
Lilim Temptation.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:17.200
Checkmate.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:24.790
Take a look at <i>that</i> .

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:30.700
What it sees now is being projected as a
hologram over Gideon and the royal capital.

00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.620
Why would you do that?

00:12:32.620 --> 00:12:37.330
One: To snap this nation's very spirit in two.

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:42.040
For that, I need the folks they rely on to
have no choice but to play into my hands,

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:46.040
then show them all how useless
the Duel City really is.

00:12:46.040 --> 00:12:48.500
The idea turns my stomach.

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:54.620
Two: To publicly humiliate the ones
who've been hot on my heels.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.750
You're one twisted piece of work.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.330
Well, the test is over.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:01.160
Do you get it, Ray?

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:03.750
Yeah. The situation's pretty grim.

00:13:03.750 --> 00:13:06.330
If only we hadn't fought at the western gate...

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:11.290
Now I can't even use Hellish
Miasma. Or the other one.

00:13:11.290 --> 00:13:12.870
Right.

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:18.080
All we can do is try ending things
with Vengeance, like always, but...

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:19.290
Ray?

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:22.660
Ladies and gentlemen!

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:26.790
It's time for the climax of my little game!

00:13:26.790 --> 00:13:31.160
This here is the switch that will release
all the monsters in town.

00:13:31.160 --> 00:13:37.750
It's configured to set every last
monster free in 652 seconds.

00:13:37.750 --> 00:13:39.660
Please, wait! If you do that--

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:43.040
So! You see this switch, yes? Well...

00:13:43.040 --> 00:13:44.370
Whoopsie!

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:52.290
Now the only way to stop me
is by defeating the RSK.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:56.250
Joining today's battle for
the Duel City's future are...

00:13:56.250 --> 00:13:59.200
...Lady Grandria and Sir Lindos.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:04.500
Plus the only Master we have
with us here today: Ray Starling!

00:14:04.500 --> 00:14:09.540
So when the city's gone, blame these three!

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.290
This guy's a colossal jerk!

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:17.450
Ray! That light is followed by an attack!

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:22.160
This might just work!

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:27.080
For sure--if I keep charging up my damage
total like this and unleash Vengeance.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.910
And yet... I can't shake this uneasiness.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:33.370
There might be more to that <i>thing</i>
than meets the eye. Still...

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:38.120
The barrier on this little baby I'm
riding here is linked to the RSK,

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:42.200
so you'll have to take down
the RSK to save the princess.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.370
Then we have no choice.

00:14:44.370 --> 00:14:45.790
Right. Let's do this!

00:14:45.790 --> 00:14:46.870
Aye-aye!

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:53.160
Your damage total...

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.870
What's wrong, Nemesis?

00:14:54.870 --> 00:14:58.910
You <i>are</i> stockpiling damage from
that monster, that's for certain...

00:14:58.910 --> 00:15:01.290
But it feels scattered somehow.

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.910
Let's try it out.

00:15:02.910 --> 00:15:05.450
The damage done will be far from fatal.

00:15:05.450 --> 00:15:08.700
I'd rather make absolutely certain now
than risk something unexpected

00:15:08.700 --> 00:15:11.120
when we try to finish it off.

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:14.790
Vengeance is Mine!

00:15:17.290 --> 00:15:18.700
Impossible!

00:15:21.330 --> 00:15:22.540
But how?

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:25.040
Oh, man, that look on your face!

00:15:25.040 --> 00:15:26.830
Franklin!

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:33.370
"But how? But why? But Vengeance is our
ultimate skill that works on <i>everybody</i> !"

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.250
That sound about right?

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:40.410
This is exactly the same as the Animal Ear
Drug you guzzled down the other day.

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:44.080
And the slime I gave you
is exactly the same, too.

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:48.540
This little fella hangs out inside your body
for 24 hours before it's digested.

00:15:48.540 --> 00:15:51.830
While it's in there,
it's continuously transmitting

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:56.450
your status and skill info, along with
your speech audio data, to me.

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:57.450
What?!

00:15:57.450 --> 00:16:02.660
You and your Embryo's skills,
gear, learnable battle moves--

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:06.580
your battle with Gouz-Maise
taught me <i>everything</i> .

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:10.950
And <i>none</i> of your skills or attacks
will work on the RSK.

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:15.620
Against you, the RSK is unbeatable
and all-powerful. After all...

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:20.870
...the Ray Starling Killer <i>was</i> made to kill <i>you</i> .

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:25.580
What gives? Why would a Superior
go to such extremes to take me down?

00:16:25.580 --> 00:16:30.410
Well, you see...
I lost to you once already.

00:16:30.410 --> 00:16:32.830
You did? To me?

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:38.700
You crushed the plan to assassinate <i>her</i> ,
so I came up with some countermeasures.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:42.580
Without you, that bear-dude
wouldn't have been there, either,

00:16:42.580 --> 00:16:47.080
and those 50 Demi-Drag-Worms
would have finished her off for sure.

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:51.000
<i>You</i> ruined my plan, and <i>you</i> handed me defeat.

00:16:51.000 --> 00:16:54.370
Bear-dude? Demi-Drag?

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.120
The man with glasses, he gave me repellent.

00:16:57.120 --> 00:17:00.910
He said that would let me go pick
remberries in the orchard.

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:03.040
I get it now.

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:06.700
I won't put up with anyone who makes me lose.

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:10.250
I won't put up with anyone who makes me yield.

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:12.580
So <i>you</i> did that.

00:17:12.580 --> 00:17:15.080
Ah, you finally understand.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:20.080
Yeah--I understand that I have to <i>hit</i> you!

00:17:20.080 --> 00:17:21.200
Say what?

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:22.870
A thought I had back then:

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:27.910
"A guy who'd send a kid to such a
dangerous place needs a good smack!"

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:30.080
And that's just what you're going to get!

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.290
Say your prayers, Superior!

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:35.120
Give it your best shot, rookie!

00:17:37.540 --> 00:17:42.750
To defeat that thing, we need to find out
why Vengeance doesn't work on it.

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.830
I have an idea about that.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.620
Eh?

00:17:45.620 --> 00:17:47.500
Now to see if I'm right!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:48.750
Ray?!

00:17:55.550 --> 00:17:58.090
"Evil Offspring"

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:58.120
I thought as much.

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.660
Force Heal!

00:18:08.620 --> 00:18:11.500
You idiot! This is practically suicide!

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:13.580
I saw a name in the light.

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.500
A name?

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:17.580
Yeah: The name display for a different monster.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:19.120
You don't mean--

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.000
<i>That</i> is not the monster that's attacking.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:26.120
But the RSK was the only thing
he summoned with his Call!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:31.160
Then maybe the RSK created a monster
inside itself <i>after</i> it was Called.

00:18:31.160 --> 00:18:33.250
What would be the point?

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:36.500
It's clear enough to me.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:40.000
One peculiarity of damage-countering skills

00:18:40.000 --> 00:18:44.950
is that they <i>only</i> work against
the enemy that dealt the damage.

00:18:44.950 --> 00:18:47.950
<i>You're</i> a sharp one.

00:18:47.950 --> 00:18:51.080
Not that it matters at all
that you've figured it out.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.370
I'm just glad there's a reason it's not working.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.250
Even a Superior like you

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:01.040
wouldn't've been able to create a monster
that's invincible for no reason.

00:19:01.040 --> 00:19:03.250
Which means there might be a way.

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:05.830
Even if it's infinitely close to zero...

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:10.660
If there's any possibility there at all,
I won't give up on grabbing hold of it!

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:16.000
That's all well and good, but what can
you do in these last 270 seconds, exactly?

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:18.160
I can beat that thing.

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:22.250
Nemesis... there's one way to turn this around.

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:23.540
You mean, <i>that</i> ?

00:19:23.540 --> 00:19:28.540
That slime was active for 24 hours,
which means Franklin won't know about it.

00:19:28.540 --> 00:19:30.040
Right.

00:19:30.040 --> 00:19:33.830
Combine that with one more gamble
and we just might win.

00:19:33.830 --> 00:19:35.500
The risk is great, though.

00:19:35.500 --> 00:19:37.950
Even greater than losing?

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.330
Good point.

00:19:39.330 --> 00:19:41.410
There's just one problem:

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.830
Our plan won't work unless
we get them out of there.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.620
You have a plan, eh?

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:49.790
We'll help.

00:19:52.410 --> 00:19:55.410
Understood. Leave the rescue to me!

00:19:55.410 --> 00:19:57.910
And I'll keep it in one place.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.620
Thanks in advance!

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.950
Now it's <i>our</i> turn!

00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:05.040
Silver! Wind Hoof, activate!

00:20:05.040 --> 00:20:06.330
Why now?

00:20:06.330 --> 00:20:10.040
Gouz-Maise! Release your MP!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:16.910
Where on earth did he get all that Grudge?

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:21.410
Is he making MP out of the fear of the
tens of thousands of people in this city--

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:23.750
fear stoked by the game <i>I</i> started?

00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:43.870
RSK, move! Get away from there!

00:20:43.870 --> 00:20:46.000
Grand Cross!

00:20:50.540 --> 00:20:51.500
Tch! Call--

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:53.500
Wind Hoof, cancel!

00:20:55.000 --> 00:21:00.200
Using tons of MP to compress a massive
chunk of air, then releasing at all at once?!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:08.700
Break on through, Silver!

00:21:16.120 --> 00:21:18.330
Gardranda!

00:21:18.330 --> 00:21:22.000
It's no use! I told you,
your skills won't work on it.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:25.370
Can it nullify <i>every</i> attack--
no matter <i>where</i> it hits?

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:28.540
I suppose you wouldn't tell me if it could.

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:30.370
Because <i>you</i> are a <i>jerk</i> .

00:21:30.370 --> 00:21:33.160
It's pointless--

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.160
Let's just see about that, shall we?

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:34.910
Wait--

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:34.910
Purgatorial Flames!

00:21:34.910 --> 00:21:37.040
Full blast!

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:44.290
Okay, my natural enemy...
who can hold out the longest?

00:23:44.440 --> 00:23:48.400
"King of Destruction"

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:47.830
"King of Destruction."
